  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response and Assistance to Displaced Persons (DP) in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to provide integrated multisectoral lifesaving and life-sustaining assistance to vulnerable populations affected by the Syrian crisis. IOM&apos;s programs are needs-driven, rights-based, and gender-, age-, and vulnerability-sensitive. IOM will maintain a strong focus on humanitarian principals and accountability throughout the project. The project will also address the immediate humanitarian needs of those affected by the crisis in Syria, while supporting longer-term resilience. IOM works with a network of partners, and ensures its actions are coordinated at all levels with relevant stakeholders and interagency forums. This project will particularly focus on the shelter, non-food items, water, sanitation and hygiene, camp coordination and camp management, protection and livelihood needs of affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
